 - Remote access: the maintainer's laptop reaches the box over SSH (`bc250` alias, key-based). Root is limited to the read-only commands in `/etc/sudoers.d/bc5-claude` (dmesg, drop_caches, `bc250-cu-live-manager status`, `amdgpu_firmware_info`). Idle suspend is prevented by the user unit `bc5-keep-awake.service` (a permanent `kde-inhibit --power --screenSaver`) plus `~/.config/powerdevilrc` `AutoSuspendAction=0`; PowerDevil only reads that file after `systemctl --user restart plasma-powerdevil`. Check with `busctl --user call org.freedesktop.PowerManagement /org/freedesktop/PowerManagement/Inhibit org.freedesktop.PowerManagement.Inhibit HasInhibit` (expect `true`). The BC-250 does not resume reliably from s2idle; Wake-on-LAN is disabled on `enp4s0` (MAC a8:a1:59:b5:ed:fe). Work directories go under `~/bc5-work` on the NVMe, not `/tmp` (tmpfs, fills up). Since 2026-10-25 the box logs the maintainer's user straight into Plasma (Wayland) at boot (`/etc/plasmalogin.conf.d/90-bc5-autologin.conf`, by `tools/scripts/autologin-setup/install.sh`; the leftover first-boot autologin of `plasma-setup` failed every boot; undo: `sudo bash ~/bc5-work/autologin-setup/undo.sh`), so after a power cut the launchers work without anyone at the box; `tools/scripts/bc5-power-cycle.py` (laptop) is the remote power-cycle through a Tuya plug, once the plug is set up. Since 2026-10-27 systemd feeds the board's hardware watchdog (SP5100 TCO, `RuntimeWatchdogSec=30s`) and the kernel reboots 10 s after a panic, an oops or a soft/hard lockup (`tools/scripts/watchdog-setup`, installed by the maintainer; undo `sudo bash ~/bc5-work/watchdog-setup/undo.sh`): a hard hang now reboots the box by itself, and autologin brings the desktop back. Two more, installed by the maintainer on 2026-10-27: efi-pstore keeps a panic's kernel log (`tools/scripts/pstore-setup`; records copied to `~/bc5-data/captures/pstore/`), and `bc5-gpu-watch.service` (`tools/scripts/gpu-watch-setup`) crashes the kernel through SysRq for a reboot when an amdgpu ring timeout or GPU reset is not followed by a successful reset within 60 s, because this kernel has no hung-task detector and PID 1 kept the hardware watchdog fed through a 26-minute stall; its lines are in `sudo dmesg`, not in `journalctl -k`.
 - Known BC-250 hazards: RADV disables the gfx1013 compute queue, but the kernel's compute rings run dispatches correctly and the direct path uses compute ring 0 for the second title (F177, F178, ADR 0009); a GPU reset can take the whole machine down — save work before running anything with `--submit`.
